{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1480168772,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxOTE4MDczNTI=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1143","origin":"github"},"title":"Switch everything to v6 repos ASAP","message":"I played with git annex on windows for a while, and it led me back to the realization that we need to switch all logic to v6 mode repositories ASAP. The possibility to have mixtures of locked an unlocked files, the option to have adjusted branch whose content needs to get `annex sync`'ed at some point put an additional level of complexity on the program logic -- which we are completely ignoring now. I think the longer we wait with this switch, the more we have to redo again.\n\nFor the record, here are a few pointers with essential information:\n\n- https://git-annex.branchable.com/tips/unlocked_files/\n- https://git-annex.branchable.com/git-annex-adjust/\n- https://git-annex.branchable.com/git-annex-sync/\n\nWe already have a few bugs with infos and issues:\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues?q=v6+label%3Aannex-v6","files":null}]}